16503	{"artifactId":"LLD-e62a9269a7cb9550-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-e62a9269a7cb9550-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:23:46.815Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac1/ac2: end() in a finally around the existing `await run` in startTurn runs exactly once for a turn that completed, failed, was stopped or was superseded, so the end-of-turn rule covers documents that became pending without a pendingApproval tool result.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1354-1356 is the single `const run = turns.start(s, req, sink); started(); await run;` site. turn-lifecycle.ts:242-255 start() awaits run() in try/finally; run() returns on every path: lock wait dropped (227, 235-238), aborted setup (321), detach (338), output ended (339-358), superseded terminal (365-369), terminal (375-383), and a throwing sink/adapter is caught at 386-393. The two early returns that refuse a message are chat-panel.ts:1199 and 1202, before turns.start. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"None. Note for the builder: a detach (window reload / chat switch, turn-lifecycle.ts:329-334) also resolves `run`, so end() fires then while the CLI keeps writing; the lazily begun followed turn takes over from its first event, as the design states.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac3: when the review pane is not available the chat host gets no presenter and behaves as today.","evidence":"extension.ts builds the chat host (567-638) and the review host (668-703) inside the same insrc.chat.enabled block, so there is no runtime state with a chat host and no review host; with the flag off neither exists. An optional deps.presenter that is absent leaves startTurn/followLiveTurn untouched. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"State in the LLD that the 'no presenter' case is the chat-disabled case (no chat host either), so the wiring test 'there is no presenter when the review pane is not created' asserts the source gate, not a runtime branch.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A superseded turn's events never reach its sink (turn-lifecycle.ts:361-374 drops them before sink.onEvent).","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts:365-372: `if (!isCurrent(myGen)) { if (isTerminal(ev)) { endTurn(ev, it); trySave(s); break; } continue; }` precedes `sink.onEvent(ev)` at 374. The superseded loop keeps reading until its terminal event, then run() returns, so the old turn's `await run` resolves after the newer turn began. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"followLiveTurn is asked for on every webview 'ready', and turns.follow returns without following while this window runs the turn, so a presented turn must begin lazily on the first follow event.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1436-1442 `case 'ready': ... postInitialState();` and postInitialState ends with `followLiveTurn(session)` at 691 (also called on a chat switch at 1505). turn-lifecycle.ts:403: `if (live === undefined || following?.sessionId === s.id || runningTurns.has(live.cursor.turnId)) return;` and 404 returns when another live window owns it. The follow sink has onEvent/onEnd(outcome) (chat-panel.ts:619-644), with outcome 'ended' | 'failed'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The review host's createPanel in extension.ts creates the pane with ViewColumn.Active today, one createPanel serves every open, and review-wiring.test.ts lines 118-120 pin that source.","evidence":"extension.ts:670-671 `createPanel: ({ viewType, title }) => { const panel = vscode.window.createWebviewPanel(viewType, title, vscode.ViewColumn.Active, { enableScripts: true });`. review-wiring.test.ts:118 regex `/createPanel: \\(\\{ viewType, title \\}\\) => \\{([\\s\\S]*?)\\n      \\},/` and 120 matches the exact createWebviewPanel line. docs-review-panel.ts:2349-2368 open() reveals an existing channel or calls deps.createPanel; openArtifact (2369-2372) calls host.open() then openArtifactFrom. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/review-wiring.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None; the Story restates the test as the design says (the destructured `{ viewType, title }` parameter in the regex changes too once `quiet` is read).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A pendingApproval.artifactPath and the pending list's mdPath are the same absolute path for the same document, so an equality match finds it.","evidence":"synthesize.ts:109-110 `pendingApproval: { artifactPath: paths.md` with paths from pathsForWorkflow (storage.ts:889); e.g. lldArtifactPaths (storage.ts:710) returns `resolveArtifactMdPath(repoPath, deriveWorkItemIdentity(epicHash, createdAtISO, storyId), 'LLD', workItemKind, epicSlug ?? epicHash)`. pending.ts:188-196 deriveMdPath calls the same resolveArtifactMdPath(repoPath, identity, kind, workItemKind, slug) with `slug = meta.epicSlug ?? hash`; path-scheme.ts:106/138 join from repoPath, so both are absolute. pendingApproval is emitted only at synthesize.ts:109. [files: src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/path-scheme.ts]","action":"None for DEF/HLD/LLD/PLAN. The match assumes the plugin's workspace folder is the repo the tool ran on (docs-review-client.ts:98-101 sends the folder as repo).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.5","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The equality match also holds for a brainstorm SPEC.","evidence":"storage.ts:911-915 writes a brainstorm SPEC with workItemKind forced to 'standalone' (`specArtifactPaths(repoPath, specHash, createdAtISO, 'standalone', epicSlug)`), while pending.ts:192 derives the kind from the record: `meta['standalone'] === true ? 'standalone' : 'epic'`. I did not read where the SPEC's meta is stamped, so I could not confirm meta.standalone is true on a SPEC; if it is not, the list path is under docs/epics and neither the equality nor the '/'-tail tolerance matches. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"Check a SPEC's meta.standalone. If it can be absent, the SPEC is still opened by the end-of-turn rule (its id is new), only later than at the tool result; say so in the edge cases or match on the artifact id as a second key.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"pendingDocuments(), review-presenter.ts / createReviewPresenter and a preserveFocus reveal do not exist yet in the plugin.","evidence":"Grep for `pendingDocuments|review-presenter|createReviewPresenter|preserveFocus` over vscode-plugin/src returns no files. DocsReviewClient (docs-review-client.ts:55-71) has only pending(), content(), decide(); pending() maps to DocsArtifactSummary and drops mdPath, keeping it only in the private mdPathById map (104, 117). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The plugin's vscode.d.ts lacks the showOptions object form and reveal's preserveFocus, and may already have ViewColumn.Beside.","evidence":"vscode.d.ts:60-65 `enum ViewColumn { Active = -1, Beside = -2, One = 1, Two = 2 }` (Beside is present); :88 `reveal(viewColumn?: ViewColumn): void;`; :129-134 createWebviewPanel takes `showOptions: ViewColumn`. extension.ts:625 already uses ViewColumn.Beside for the chat panel. [files: vscode-plugin/src/vscode.d.ts]","action":"None; only the two declarations are added.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A 'tool-result' turn event carries the tool's text in `output` and `isError`, and a workflow tool's result text is JSON carrying the pendingApproval block.","evidence":"stream-events.ts:82-85 `kind: 'tool-result'; turnId; command?; output: string`. cli-adapter.ts:639-650 builds it from claude's tool_result block: `output = coerceToolResultOutput(block['content'])` (267-275 joins the text blocks) and `isError: true` when `is_error`. The MCP server returns the result as one text block of JSON (server.ts:1074/1122 `JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)`; step tools forward the daemon's text at 1042). Not confirmed: that the CLI passes a very large result (the synthesize result carries `markdown` and `artifact`, synthesize.ts:103-107) through whole; a clipped or file-redirected result would not parse. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/stream-events.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, src/mcp/server.ts]","action":"Keep the end-of-turn rule as the stated fallback for a result that does not parse; the design's edge case 'a tool result is large' should say the fallback applies when the CLI does not pass the text whole.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Making ChatPanelChannel.reveal take an optional argument leaves every existing caller and implementer unchanged, and webview-channel.ts is the one production implementer.","evidence":"Interface at chat-panel.ts:49 `reveal(): void;`. One production implementer: webview-channel.ts:43 `reveal: () => panel.reveal()`. Callers: chat-panel.ts:1748, board-host.ts:721, docs-review-panel.ts:2352, all `channel.reveal()`. extension.ts:342 and panels/webview-host.ts:172/179 belong to the separate panels/types.ts:110 interface. A zero-argument fake still satisfies the widened signature. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/webview-channel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"Name in the LLD that WebviewPanelLike.reveal (webview-channel.ts:22, `reveal(): void`) is widened to `reveal(viewColumn?: unknown, preserveFocus?: boolean)` in the same file, or `panel.reveal(undefined, true)` does not typecheck.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding optional `quiet` to openArtifact's target and createPanel's opts does not break the delivery board's callers.","evidence":"board-host.ts:61 and details-memory.ts:62 declare `reviewPane?: { openArtifact(target: { readonly artifactId: string; readonly mdPath: string }): void }` structurally, and details-memory.ts:173 calls `openArtifact({ artifactId, mdPath: entry.mdPath })`; a host method that also accepts an optional `quiet` is assignable. DocsReviewHostDeps.createPanel is at docs-review-panel.ts:35 with one production caller (2356) and one provider (extension.ts:670). [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"extension.ts can pass a presenter to createChatPanelHost that is wired to the review host's openArtifact and the review client's pendingDocuments.","evidence":"It can, but the design does not name two things the wiring needs: the chat host is constructed at extension.ts:567, before the review host at 668, and the review client is created inline as the review host's `client` at 669 with no binding of its own. The reverse link already uses a late-bound closure (`notifyChat: (text) => chatHost.submitExternal(text)`, 697). [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"Add to step 4: hoist `createDocsReviewClient(...)` to a const above the chat host (or make a second client; pendingDocuments keeps no state), and have the presenter's `open` close over a `let reviewHost` assigned after it is built, since the presenter is only called during a turn.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Nothing stored changes: the presenter is called beside, not inside, the path that writes transcript rows and posts events, and no daemon call or shape is added.","evidence":"Rows and posts are made by `appendEvent(s, ev)` / `postLive(ev, rowIndex)` in the run sink (chat-panel.ts:1289-1291) and the follow sink (624-629); a toolResult(ev.output) call ahead of them reads the event only. pendingDocuments reuses the existing `workflow.pending` RPC and PendingArtifact.mdPath (pending.ts:46), where '' means unresolvable (docs-review-client.ts:115-117 already skips it), so no IPC shape changes and an older daemon answers the same call. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A presenter that throws must be caught by the chat host's own wrapper, because an uncaught throw in the run sink's onEvent would fail the turn.","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts:374 calls `sink.onEvent(ev)` unguarded inside the try whose catch (386-393) does `finishIterator(iterator)` and `reportError(sink, ...)`: a throw there ends the turn as an error. Only the follow path guards it (437-441, logs 'an event was not handled'). The design wraps every presenter call in the host and has the presenter return at once and never throw, with failed reads and a throwing open logged; that is sufficient for both paths. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"None. Keep the wrapper around begin() too: it sits before turns.start, where a throw would reject runTurn, which is fired with `void`.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to named tests that can be written in the plugin's existing test files and style.","evidence":"The acceptance table maps ac1, ac2 and ac3 each to unit and integration subjects. The test files they extend exist: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, docs-review-client.test.ts, docs-review-panel.test.ts, review-wiring.test.ts, turn-lifecycle.test.ts. Every seam under test is injected (createPanel, client, channel, turns via providers), so quiet/preserveFocus is observable on a fake. I did not read the fakes inside those tests. 'The chat keeps keyboard focus' in a real window is covered only by the hand check, which is the most a node test can do here. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/review-wiring.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-client.test.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-13T17:23:46.815Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
